# The context is everything this image needs and nothing else: `*` excludes the whole module -
# src/, the Gradle build directory, the README - and each line below adds back one file the
# Dockerfile actually COPYs. That means a new COPY needs a line here, or the build fails with
# `failed to compute cache key: "/<file>": not found` and nothing points at this file. That is
# exactly how it went wrong once in discord-bot, on 2026-09-02.
*
!build/libs/*.jar
!docker-entrypoint.sh

# ...and the thin jar back out again. THIS LINE IS LOAD-BEARING, not tidiness. The Dockerfile picks
# its jar with a glob rather than being told a version, and `shadowJar` leaves updater-<v>.jar
# and updater-<v>-thin.jar side by side, so without this both match.
#
# Two matches is not a build failure. Measured on 2026-09-09 with Docker 29.7.2: BuildKit copies one
# of them into the destination and reports nothing. The one it picked was the right one only because
# `-thin.jar` sorts before `.jar`. Relying on that would mean an image that one day silently carries
# the dependency-less jar and dies on the first class it cannot find.
build/libs/*-thin.jar
